# SHA-256 of every upstream file this package ships — two of which this fork
# patched on purpose, as the header records below — plus the independent fixture
# its tests read, from IUPAC/InChI v1.07.5 (tag v1.07.5, commit
# 11a87982bb518f57ac013f0b258c283655e1ea1d,
# https://github.com/IUPAC/InChI.git).
#
# 110 records:
#
#   105 files   the two upstream-owned directories of build.zig.zon `.paths`,
#               INCHI-1-SRC/INCHI_BASE/src (86 files) and
#               INCHI-1-SRC/INCHI_API/libinchi/src (19 files). This is the
#               complete compile unit list of that CMake target plus every
#               header reached from them by #include, the two public headers
#               that are installed (inchi_api.h, ixa.h), the bundled stb_sprintf
#               1.10, the SHA-256 implementation, and upstream's own
#               CMakeLists.txt for the target. It is a subset of the upstream
#               tree, not a copy of it: upstream also ships the inchi-1
#               executable, the demos, the vc14 and gcc project files, the
#               documentation and the test distribution, none of which this
#               package builds or needs.
#
#   103 files   of those 105 are upstream's own bytes, byte for byte.
#     2 files    INCHI-1-SRC/INCHI_BASE/src/ichiparm.c and
#               INCHI-1-SRC/INCHI_BASE/src/ichicano.c, which this fork edited
#               once each, on purpose, and discloses here.
#
#     1 file    ichiparm.c. The patch is nine inserted lines -- a seven-line
#               disclosure comment and two string-literal macros -- plus three
#               changed lines: two banner arguments in HelpCommandLineParms
#               where the compiler's build-date and build-time macros were, now
#               the pinned source tag and a literal no-timestamp string, and one
#               existing comment line whose format string held an accidental
#               nested-comment delimiter. The diagnostics that prompted it were
#               fixed at their cause; nothing was suppressed, no flag was added,
#               and no chemistry, ABI, allocator, option or timeout behaviour was
#               touched. Upstream's digest for this file,
#               eb3516115a1d25776f823de800d1c61cf0161e5bedbecac3511cd21ec0de2478,
#               is preserved in UPSTREAM.md as the baseline the patch is
#               measured against; the record below is of this fork's bytes,
#               because those are the bytes the build compiles.
#
#     1 file    ichicano.c. The patch moves the file's `#include
#               <sys/timeb.h>` below `#include "mode.h"` and wraps it in
#               `#ifndef COMPILE_ANSI_ONLY` / `#endif`. Compared with upstream,
#               those two guard lines add 33 bytes. Compared with the first
#               guard version, only placement changes: the file stays 107427
#               bytes and no line number from line 53 down moves.
#               Placement is the patch. `mode.h:197-201` defines
#               COMPILE_ANSI_ONLY itself for every non-Microsoft compiler and
#               for TARGET_API_LIB, so a guard read above `#include "mode.h"`
#               sees the macro still undefined and includes the header anyway;
#               that was the defect in the first version of this patch, and the
#               file failed to preprocess with `-DTARGET_API_LIB=1` and
#               succeeded with `-DCOMPILE_ANSI_ONLY=1`
#               (local://foundation-cross-test-inchi-guard.json). The header is
#               not missing from every non-Windows libc: of seven probes
#               (local://foundation-cross-test-timeb-header-availability.json)
#               it is present on x86_64-linux-gnu, x86_64-linux-musl,
#               x86_64-netbsd and wasm32-wasi, present on aarch64-freebsd with a
#               deprecation warning, and absent only on aarch64-macos and
#               x86_64-openbsd. The whole translation unit that uses it -
#               InchiTimeGet and bInchiTimeIsOver, the only two readers of
#               `struct _timeb` and `_ftime`, at pre-patch lines 332-335 and
#               395-402 - sits in the `#else` arm of this same file's
#               `#ifdef COMPILE_ANSI_ONLY` at pre-patch line 95, so the guard
#               removes a header nothing in that configuration uses and changes
#               no compiled token in any other one. Upstream's own header
#               agrees: ichitime.h:56 carries the same include commented out
#               under the same macro. Upstream's digest for this file,
#               5c031a2b441dc08509f75fe22e4b6ecddf285ada625b4a69cf77d2920d42f891,
#               is preserved in UPSTREAM.md as the baseline; the record below is
#               of this fork's bytes, because those are the bytes the build
#               compiles.
#
#     1 file    LICENSE, the MIT text, verbatim.
#     1 file    README.upstream.md, upstream's own project README, verbatim.
#               Upstream's README lives at the repository root, where a Zig
#               package needs its own README.md; the upstream bytes are
#               preserved under this name and the record names this path. The
#               digest below is unchanged by the move, because the bytes are.
#     1 file    INCHI-1-SRC/INCHI_API/libinchi/gcc/libinchi.map, upstream's own
#               ELF version script: the exported-symbol list for a shared
#               libinchi, naming the public API and nothing else. It moved from
#               "carried for provenance" into `.paths` when this fork began
#               producing a real shared library, because a shared build passes
#               it to the linker and a build cannot read a file the package
#               does not ship. It is upstream's file, unmodified, and it is
#               read only on ELF targets and only when -Dlinkage=dynamic.
#     1 file    INCHI-1-SRC/INCHI_API/tbb/LICENSE, upstream's full Apache-2.0
#               terms for the uncompiled proxy header shipped with the source.
#     1 file    testdata/pubchem_known_answers.tsv, the independent known
#               answers. Not upstream's and not this fork's: every field was
#               read out of PubChem's own compound records, queried one CID at
#               a time through the PUG REST property endpoint, as the file's
#               own header records. It is hashed here because the tests embed
#               it and a silent edit to it would move every published
#               expectation in the package at once.
#
# Deliberately absent, each for a stated reason:
#   build.zig, build.zig.zon, translate.h, zig/, tests.zig, smoke.zig,
#   cross-test.profile.sh, consumer/ and UPSTREAM.md, NOTICE.md, CHANGELOG.md,
#   FORK-NOTES.md, FORK-LICENSE.md, README.md, README.zig.md -- this fork's own
#   files, listed in NOTICE.md. README.md is this fork's own document; upstream's
#   README is the record immediately above, under its preserved path.
#   package.nix, flake.nix, devenv.nix, devenv.yaml, .envrc and flake.lock --
#   this fork's own portable-packaging files, listed in NOTICE.md. flake.lock
#   is a real committed file here and build.zig.zon lists it in .paths, but the
#   records above cover upstream's files only, so no fork-authored metadata is
#   hashed: it pins this fork's own nixpkgs input, not upstream's bytes.
#   devenv.lock does not exist in this repository and none is invented to fill
#   the slot.
#   .gitignore -- upstream's ignore rules are kept verbatim and this fork
#   appends its own Zig entries below them, so the file is not byte-identical
#   to upstream's.
#   .github/, .devcontainer/, .editorconfig, .gitattributes, .dockerignore,
#   Doxyfile, INCHI-1-DOC/, INCHI-1-TEST/ and the whole of INCHI-1-SRC except
#   the two src directories, INCHI-1-SRC/INCHI_API/tbb/LICENSE and the one file
#   INCHI-1-SRC/INCHI_API/libinchi/gcc/libinchi.map -- carried in this
#   repository for provenance and re-sync diffs, and not in `.paths`. The
#   version script is the exception that stopped being an exception; the
#   makefiles beside it still are, because the build reads its flags from
#   build.zig rather than from them.
#   UPSTREAM.sha256 itself -- a record cannot contain its own digest.
#
# These are the bytes in this working tree, hashed as a raw byte read (Bun
# File.arrayBuffer, SHA-256 from node:crypto). They are not a signature and not
# a Git object id: see UPSTREAM.md, "Integrity", for what they do and do not
# establish.
#
# Provenance of the numbers: the 108 records other than the ichiparm.c line were
# written on 2026-10-01, and every one of them was re-derived from this written
# file and compared against it, 108 of 108 matching. The 109th line, the
# Apache-2.0 text, was added afterwards. The ichiparm.c line is the one record
# the first disclosed patch changed: it was re-derived from the patched file's own
# bytes, and then all 109 records were re-derived from disk and compared
# against this file, with that line and no other differing.
#
# The ichicano.c line changed twice. The first change wrapped the include in
# `#ifndef COMPILE_ANSI_ONLY` where the file had it, above `#include "mode.h"`,
# which guarded nothing: mode.h defines the macro later in the same
# translation unit, so the include was still processed and the macOS cell still
# failed. The line was then re-derived from the reordered file's own bytes.
# The upstream baseline it is measured against was re-derived in the same pass,
# by deleting the three guard lines and restoring the include at upstream's own
# position 46: the result hashes to the 5c031a2b… digest quoted above, and it is
# 107394 bytes, so the 107427 the record names adds exactly 33 guard bytes.
# The two-source patch shape and the 109 paths remain unchanged.
# The ichiparm.c disclosure comment was clarified in three existing lines;
# its new digest below covers 111263 bytes. Source-line count and every
# noncomment byte are unchanged, observed in the external comment-only proof.
# Current source/fetched replay status is driver-owned under
# FORKS.json.cross_test_wave.materialized_packages.inchi.
#
# `sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256` was green over all 109 of these bytes in two
# receipts, and both of them are history for this file now: each verified the
# `ichicano.c` line as it stood before the guarded include described above.
#   local://foundation-expansion-inchi-authorized-patch-integrity-109-364.log
#     exit 0, 109 records, 109 ": OK", no failures
#   local://foundation-expansion-inchi-current-filtered-package-integrity-388.log
#     exit 0, 109 records, 109 ": OK", no failures, over the .paths-filtered
#     copy materialised from a current `zig fetch` of this package
# The pre-patch receipts (…-240 over 109 records, …-221 and …-127 over 108)
# remain history; their ichiparm.c lines verified upstream's bytes, which this
# record no longer names.
#
# Verify with:  sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256
